  "row_count": 21,
  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 1210.4 K, melting point of Ge; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 8.830$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 14.653 + 0.150 \\times 10^{-3} T - 1.432 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$$\n\\mathrm{H} ^ {0} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {0} = 1 4. 6 5 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 0. 0 7 5 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 1. 4 3 2 \\times 1 0 ^ {2} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} - 4. 8 5 6\n$$\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1210.4 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -16.132 + 0.729 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.711 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 50 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$$\n\\Delta G r ^ {0} = - 1 6. 1 3 2 - 0. 7 2 9 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} + 0. 7 1 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 2 5. 0 0 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 2. 9 1 4 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T}\n$$\n1210.4-2000 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -24.432 - 0.290 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.245 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 74.900 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$$\n\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr} ^ {\\circ} = - 2 4. 4 3 2 + 0. 2 9 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 9} \\mathrm{TlnT} + 0. 2 4 5 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 3 7. 4 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 3. 0 9 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T}\n$$\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K based on Karbanov (61). Other data are from Gurvich (49). ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "Phase change: 1210.4 K, melting point of Ge; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 8.830$ kcal/mol.",
      "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations:",
      "298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 14.653 + 0.150 \\times 10^{-3} T - 1.432 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$",
      "$$",
      "\\mathrm{H} ^ {0} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {0} = 1 4. 6 5 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 0. 0 7 5 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 1. 4 3 2 \\times 1 0 ^ {2} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} - 4. 8 5 6",
      "$$",
      "Reaction equations (kcal/mol):",
      "298.15-1210.4 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -16.132 + 0.729 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.711 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 50 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$$",
      "\\Delta G r ^ {0} = - 1 6. 1 3 2 - 0. 7 2 9 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} + 0. 7 1 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 2 5. 0 0 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 2. 9 1 4 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T}",
      "$$",
      "1210.4-2000 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -24.432 - 0.290 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.245 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 74.900 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$$",
      "\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr} ^ {\\circ} = - 2 4. 4 3 2 + 0. 2 9 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 9} \\mathrm{TlnT} + 0. 2 4 5 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 3 7. 4 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 3. 0 9 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T}",
      "$$",
      "Sources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K based on Karbanov (61). Other data are from Gurvich (49)."
    ],
